ng how they actually  compared to apple's chips while in real  workflows so because of this apple's a15  ship is untouchable for another year at  least and now before i jump into some  actually good news and brand new leaks  concerning apple's iphone 14 lineup i  want to make my final point about why  only the pro models will be getting the  a16 chip this year first of all apple  seems to be wanting to sell more pro  models and this makes sense because  that'll help them bring their average  sales price up which is very important  to their investors and the second reason  is that all of the main sources  including ming chi quo and ross young  fully believe that the new iphone lineup  will now introduce a brand new iphone 14  max model which will pack essentially  the same base feature set as the regular  14 but now with a larger 6.7 inch  display and in my opinion the regular 14  will start at 799 with a 100 price jump  up to the larger 14 max and then you'll  have to pay an extra 300  for the pro and pro max models for each  corresponding size and yes that means  that the pro models will now be a  hundred dollars more expensive compared  to last year and i'll explain why in  just a minute but the main point i want  to make is that now that apple for the  first time ever has two models with a  larger 6.7 inch display they need to  make it very clear and have clear  distinctions and differences between the  regular 14 max model and the more  expensive 14 pro max so that users can  easily tell the difference for example  we're already 100 certain that only the  pro models will be coming with the new  dual punch hole cutout on the display  while the regular 14 models including  the brand new 14 max will still have a  notch and to make things worse we've  been getting reports that the lower end  14 models will have the same display  bezels as the current 13 while the 14  pro models will get thinner bezels which  look much nicer and just yesterday  imagine boo released these new images of  the dual cutout display and it honestly  looks really really nice in my opinion  and this user even lined up the cutouts  with the current notch design and it's  clear that apple has a real winner with  these new 14 pro models but on top of  that apple is planning to have even more  differences like ross young confirming  that 120 hertz promotion will once again  be exclusive to the pro models so the  regular 14s will still be sticking to a  60 hertz display and now the last point  i want to make for why apple is only  giving the new a16 chip to the pro  models is that apple's costs for this  chip will be quite a bit higher than the  a15 first of all tsmc has already  announced that they're raising prices  for their best and latest process nodes  bringing costs up going further micciko  believes that the new a16 ships will use  faster and more expensive lp ddr5 ram  and there are rumors that the a16 will  be the first chip to use tsmc's new  expensive 3d fabric technology but the  real big problem in my opinion is that  there have been some real supply chain  issues that are putting pressure on  apple's profit margins so it makes sense  to put cheaper chips on the lower end  models while forcing users to pay more  for these brand new expensive chips and  making things even worse shenzhen china  which houses the biggest apple product  factory in the world has just gone into  full lockdown which will add to these  supply problems so with that said maybe  apple just can't afford to take the  profit margin hit by giving the lower  end iphones the latest chip especially  since inflationary and commodity price  pressures have gotten even worse over  the past couple of months but now with  the bad news out of the way let's  finally get into the good news all  iphone 14 models are expected to get a  full redesign with protruding flat glass  on both the front and the back as well  as the possibility of getting a usb-c  port but that's still uncertain and 